// The `once` library entry is special: alive for exactly one
// ath_is_alive observation, dead afterward. Putting it in an ~ATH loop
// is the natural way to write "run this body exactly one time, then
// move on" without any rebind-or-kill machinery.

import once V;
~ATH(V) {
    print exactly one run;
}
print after;
THIS.DIE();
